0352: SweetFramebuffer: scanout fixes, no frame of a surface shown half drawn, flips taken by CTL_FLUSH (kern.sweet_fb_flush_taken, default 0)

Needs 0349 and 0350. Nothing changes unless kern.sweet_fb_scanout (0350) or kern.sweet_fb_flush_taken is
switched on, except item 1, which only matters once frames of surfaces have been in the queue.

1. presentQueued() (0340) now clears the queue entry it fills: a copy queued where a scanned-out frame had
   been inherited its scan flag and was shown as one.
2. scanFrom() and planeScaled() note the flip (frame counter, line) when it is written, not before waiting
   for a writable plane; a note a refresh old let flipTaken() release a surface the panel was still reading.
3. A frame of a surface is not shown before its drawing is done (0350 showed it after 250 ms); a hung GPU is
   reset after 2 s and its fences complete (0317), as for the copies. queueDrain() drops such a frame instead.
4. CTL_FLUSH, measured with 0349 (kernel 0350, 14388 flips): its bits read set right after the write in 14386
   flips and clear at the programmable fetch (line 2420 of 2432), ~12 lines before INTF_FRAME_COUNT moves; of
   14324 flips followed, 99.5 % cleared by the counter's first move; in the second-to-last sixteenth of the
   refresh 11 of 922 cleared only at the second move. Once 16 flips have been seen and at most one in 64 read
   clear right after the write, CTL_FLUSH is taken to read back:
   - planeWritable(): bits clear are enough, at any line (Linux msm_atomic_commit_tail does no more); the line
     window of 0350 stays for a CTL_FLUSH that does not read back;
   - kern.sweet_fb_flush_taken (read-write, boot-arg sweetfb_flush_taken), default 0: flips are taken by the
     frame counter (0340), and by the bits once a scanned-out frame has been on the panel; 1: every flip,
     copies too, is taken when the bits read clear.
5. kern.sweet_fb_scanout_diag says how many flips read the bits back and which rule takes the flips.

Items 1 and 2 were found by a host simulation of the queue and scanout code extracted from the file, against
a model of the GPU, the display engine and the window server.
Measured on the phone (one boot): kern.sweet_fb_scanout=1 ran without hangs, flushes not taken 0.
kern.sweet_fb_flush_taken=1 is not measured. Off: kern.sweet_fb_scanout=0 and kern.sweet_fb_flush_taken=0.

